Half the time they won’t even wear it because they don't see no danger at all.

1800
02:00:41.000 --> 02:00:42.975
<v ARSENEAULT>Were you always an activist?

1801
02:00:42.975 --> 02:00:46.136
Like were you in the Black Panther Party?

1802
02:00:46.136 --> 02:00:52.852
<v DELMA BENNETT>I didn't join because I didn't . . . see the Muslims, the Black Panther Party, Southern Christian Leadership Association,

1803
02:00:52.852 --> 02:00:59.963
and it was another group in Los Angeles named Us that were similar to the Black Panther Party.

1804
02:00:59.963 --> 02:01:05.099
Then later on the Crips . . . the Bloods and the Crips came into existence.

1805
02:01:05.099 --> 02:01:08.259
But I associated with the Black Panther’s Party.

1806
02:01:08.259 --> 02:01:13.000
I went to the party . . . To the headquarters and stuff like that.

1807
02:01:13.000 --> 02:01:28.802
But I could never get involved in the Black Panther Party was because of the fact that I thought that the Muslims had more to offer than the Black Panther Party because the Muslim wasn't asking the society for anything.

1808
02:01:28.802 --> 02:01:35.914
All they wanted to do was have a place where they can go and do their own thing.

1809
02:01:35.914 --> 02:01:44.605
But America couldn't do that because they say, "Well it wouldn't look right for me to give . . ." Because they wanted the desert.

1810
02:01:44.605 --> 02:01:47.370
They say, "Just give us the desert.

1811
02:01:47.370 --> 02:01:49.346
We'll go stay in the

1812
02:01:49.346 --> 02:01:52.111
<c.p>desert and we'll survive in the desert."

1813
02:01:52.111 --> 02:01:59.617
But they say they couldn't do that because they fought their brothers to keep from having this country divided.

1814
02:01:59.617 --> 02:02:08.309
So why would we give you a place where you can go and set up similar to the way my brothers did?

1815
02:02:08.309 --> 02:02:16.605
Now they had to do what they did to the Indians because this was the Indians’ place in the first place.

1816
02:02:16.605 --> 02:02:24.506
So that's why they gave them territories because this was their land and they just put them in different territories.

1817
02:02:24.506 --> 02:02:31.617
So I kind of liked it that about the black . . . I mean the Muslims because they were independent.

1818
02:02:31.617 --> 02:02:33.988
Well the Black Panthers weren't independent.

1819
02:02:33.988 --> 02:02:36.753
They were similar to Klu Klux Klanmans,

1820
02:02:36.753 --> 02:02:47.025
but the only difference was they didn't have the type of power that the Klu Klux Klans had because they didn't have nobody to back them.

1821
02:02:47.025 --> 02:02:55.321
See what the Klu Klux Klans have done . . . With the things that they've done, they've always had somebody to back them.

1822
02:02:55.321 --> 02:02:58.086
And even all the way in Washington,

1823
02:02:58.086 --> 02:03:09.148
D.C. there was people that was backing them because they had Klu Klux Klans in the Senate and in the House and in all that kind of stuff.

1824
02:03:09.148 --> 02:03:12.309
So they really had somebody to back them.

1825
02:03:12.309 --> 02:03:16.259
So I couldn't go along with the Black Panther Party.

1826
02:03:16.259 --> 02:03:21.000
I appreciate what they done to show that we weren't afraid.

1827
02:03:21.000 --> 02:03:27.767
You see, because history don't teach us about the rebellion . . . Our rebellious spirit and how we rebelled against slavery.

1828
02:03:27.767 --> 02:03:30.616
See, they always taught us as being humble.

1829
02:03:30.616 --> 02:03:34.890
That we just wanted to be in the position that we're in.

1830
02:03:34.890 --> 02:03:39.877
But here we're coming from kings and queens and all this kind of stuff,

1831
02:03:39.877 --> 02:03:47.000
but all of a sudden we want to be humble and be put in this position that we're in.

1832
02:03:47.000 --> 02:03:55.230
So now with Martin Luther King, I liked that Martin Luther King because he tried to fight them with the law.

1833
02:03:55.230 --> 02:03:57.973
See that's what I liked about him.

1834
02:03:57.973 --> 02:04:08.162
To be able to have endured the things that he endured he had to have some type of backing with him other than just man itself.

1835
02:04:08.162 --> 02:04:15.216
He had to have some type of spiritual backing to allow him to have done what he done.

1836
02:04:15.216 --> 02:04:16.000
To be

1837
02:04:16.000 --> 02:04:19.135
<c.p>able to take the abuse that he took.

1838
02:04:19.135 --> 02:04:26.189
So I admired him for what he done, and he made more of a change than anybody else.

1839
02:04:26.189 --> 02:04:31.284
This other group called Us, it was similar to the Black Panther Party.

1840
02:04:31.284 --> 02:04:35.203
They had the black stone rangers and stuff in Chicago.

1841
02:04:35.203 --> 02:04:39.905
Every area had their own little rebellious groups and stuff like that.

1842
02:04:39.905 --> 02:04:47.743
The only thing that made the Panthers the way they were, they were more advertised than the rest of them.

1843
02:04:47.743 --> 02:04:56.365
And they were advertised because the fact they were on the West Coast where the media covered a whole lot of stuff.

1844
02:04:56.365 --> 02:05:01.459
Those are type of things that I was involved in in my life.

1845
02:05:01.459 --> 02:05:05.770
The greatest thing that I've ever experienced so far is Christianity.

1846
02:05:05.770 --> 02:05:15.176
I don't mean to the point to where I am . . . I mean where Christianity is because a lot of Christianity is a big farce.

1847
02:05:15.176 --> 02:05:19.486
It's not really the way God set it up to be.

1848
02:05:19.486 --> 02:05:21.446
Just like with Sunday worship.

1849
02:05:21.446 --> 02:05:23.797
Sunday worship is not of God,

1850
02:05:23.797 --> 02:05:35.946
but the whole world follow after that worship time because it was set up to actually throw people off balance thinking that this is the way it is because God said,

1851
02:05:35.946 --> 02:05:39.081
"Remember the seventh day and keep it holy."

1852
02:05:39.081 --> 02:05:41.432
The seventh day definitely isn't Sunday.

1853
02:05:41.432 --> 02:05:42.216
It's either . . . .

1854
02:05:42.216 --> 02:05:43.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Saturday?

1855
02:05:43.000 --> 02:05:43.556
<v DELMA BENNETT>It's Saturday.

1856
02:05:43.556 --> 02:05:46.333
And this is the day we're supposed to keep holy.

1857
02:05:46.333 --> 02:05:49.389
But the whole world flocks after the beast and keeps Sunday.

1858
02:05:49.389 --> 02:05:53.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Were you raised . . . how . . . What church did you go to growing up?

1859
02:05:53.000 --> 02:05:54.423
<v DELMA BENNETT>I'm Seven Day Adventist.

1860
02:05:54.423 --> 02:05:55.847
Yeah, Seven Day Adventist.

1861
02:05:55.847 --> 02:06:00.473
But we’re not the only one that keeps Sundays though, I mean Saturday.

1862
02:06:00.473 --> 02:06:02.252
We're not the only one

1863
02:06:02.252 --> 02:06:02.964
<c.p>keep Saturday.

1864
02:06:02.964 --> 02:06:05.099
There's other religions that keep Saturday.

1865
02:06:05.099 --> 02:06:10.793
There's even a seven day Baptist, Pentecostals, but people don't understand how Sunday came into existence.

1866
02:06:10.793 --> 02:06:13.284
See God didn't give us the weekend.

1867
02:06:13.284 --> 02:06:16.131
God said we supposed to work six days.

1868
02:06:16.131 --> 02:06:17.198
Not five days.

1869
02:06:17.198 --> 02:06:19.333
We supposed to work six days.

1870
02:06:19.333 --> 02:06:22.180
So Constantine came up with this weekend thing.

1871
02:06:22.180 --> 02:06:26.450
See if you keep Sunday I'm going to stop persecuting the Christians.

1872
02:06:26.450 --> 02:06:33.212
So what would you do if you say, "I'm going to give you an extra day to be off."

1873
02:06:33.212 --> 02:06:35.703
I'm going to go along with it,

1874
02:06:35.703 --> 02:06:42.820
but now Saturday become a burden because certain things I can’t do on Saturdays that I can do on Sundays.

1875
02:06:42.820 --> 02:06:47.446
But I'm still worshipping God so I'm going to go along with Sunday.

1876
02:06:47.446 --> 02:06:53.140
So most people went with Sunday instead of going with what God said, the seventh day.

1877
02:06:53.140 --> 02:06:57.054
The only way that Sunday can be the day of worship,

1878
02:06:57.054 --> 02:07:05.950
you have to be able to find it in the Bible that it was written in stone because the seventh day was written in stone.

1879
02:07:05.950 --> 02:07:10.577
It wasn't really in stone once, it was written in stone twice because . . .

1880
02:07:10.577 --> 02:07:12.000
<v ARSENEAULT>The Ten Commandments?

1881
02:07:12.000 --> 02:07:12.341
<v DELMA BENNETT>[Agrees].

1882
02:07:12.341 --> 02:07:18.136
It was written twice because when Moses broke the first tablet of stone that God gave him,

1883
02:07:18.136 --> 02:07:24.273
he had to carve two more stones and bring them back to God so he could rewrite them,

1884
02:07:24.273 --> 02:07:28.023
and God wouldn't allow no man to rewrite them but him.

1885
02:07:28.023 --> 02:07:33.818
Then all of a sudden Sunday come into existence and there's nowhere in the Bible in stone.

1886
02:07:33.818 --> 02:07:38.932
It's something that man came up with and the whole world's following after the beast.

1887
02:07:38.932 --> 02:07:42.000
<v ARSENEAULT>When did you get more involved with Christianity?

1888
02:07:42.000 --> 02:07:46.377
<v DELMA BENNETT>It was after . . . I was raised, like my wife said, I was

1889
02:07:46.377 --> 02:07:51.119
<c.p>raised Catholic and my wife and I started searching after I got married.

1890
02:07:51.119 --> 02:07:53.307
My wife and I start searching.

1891
02:07:53.307 --> 02:07:55.131
We went from different places.

1892
02:07:55.131 --> 02:07:59.143
I studied with the Muslims, Jehovah Witness, Pentecostal, Catholic, Baptist, Methodist.

1893
02:07:59.143 --> 02:08:01.332
I studied with all of them.

1894
02:08:01.332 --> 02:08:09.357
Then when I found the Seven Day Adventists . . . The way I found that out I was working at Firestone at the time,

1895
02:08:09.357 --> 02:08:14.463
and there was a guy that was a Seven Day Adventist named George Young.

1896
02:08:14.463 --> 02:08:18.475
He had lost his job because he would keep the Sabbath.

1897
02:08:18.475 --> 02:08:24.311
He wouldn't work on Friday . . . From Friday sunset to Saturday sunset, and so they fired him.

1898
02:08:24.311 --> 02:08:25.406
I said, "Hmm."

1899
02:08:25.406 --> 02:08:31.971
When I see something that impress me I think it's worth it, that's what I want to be.

1900
02:08:31.971 --> 02:08:35.254
Like I did when I was in the service.

1901
02:08:35.254 --> 02:08:38.537
And I say that's what I wanted to be.

1902
02:08:38.537 --> 02:08:43.279
So I started studying and found out what he had done was right.

1903
02:08:43.279 --> 02:08:48.020
So I just [flocked?] that in, and I learned a lot from it.

1904
02:08:48.020 --> 02:08:55.316
Coming with the eating . . . when I talk about . . . I don't know if you heard me talk about eating and stuff.

1905
02:08:55.316 --> 02:08:58.598
The things we can eat and about the scavenging.

1906
02:08:58.598 --> 02:09:00.057
I had a big . . .

1907
02:09:00.057 --> 02:09:01.152
<v ARSENEAULT>The cloven foot?

1908
02:09:01.152 --> 02:09:06.258
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yeah I was in a conversation with my acupuncturist doctor this morning about it.

1909
02:09:06.258 --> 02:09:09.906
He gave me these papers to read about the Sabbath.

1910
02:09:09.906 --> 02:09:11.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Oh, wow.

1911
02:09:11.000 --> 02:09:13.742
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yeah he gave me that this morning.

1912
02:09:13.742 --> 02:09:14.525
<v ARSENEAULT>No pork?

1913
02:09:14.525 --> 02:09:16.092
<v DELMA BENNETT>Oh, no. No pork.

1914
02:09:16.092 --> 02:09:16.875
<v ARSENEAULT>No shrimp?

1915
02:09:16.875 --> 02:09:20.792
<v DELMA BENNETT>No shrimp, no crawfish, no crab, no lobster, no catfish.

1916
02:09:20.792 --> 02:09:21.575
No, no . . .

1917
02:09:21.575 --> 02:09:22.358
<v ARSENEAULT>Bottom feeders.

1918
02:09:22.358 --> 02:09:24.317
<v DELMA BENNETT>All of them are scavengers.

1919
02:09:24.317 --> 02:09:26.275
Everything we name was scavengers.

1920
02:09:26.275 --> 02:09:28.233
A buzzard is a scavenger.

1921
02:09:28.233 --> 02:09:33.717
Now they talk about a chicken, but see the thing is chicken eat anything.

1922
02:09:33.717 --> 02:09:35.283
Anything the chicken eat.

1923
02:09:35.283 --> 02:09:41.158
But the thing is God fixed it where nothing goes into its body that's unclean.

1924
02:09:41.158 --> 02:09:48.992
He gives them a gizzard and all that food is purified in its gizzards before it goes into its body.

1925
02:09:48.992 --> 02:09:54.867
So God arranged everything, but man did it the way they wanted to do it.

1926
02:09:54.867 --> 02:09:58.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Did you have a business in Mossville?

1927
02:09:58.000 --> 02:10:00.800
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yeah I had my little jewelry business.

1928
02:10:00.800 --> 02:10:05.200
I did . . . I ran it from Mossville, and my lawn service.

1929
02:10:05.200 --> 02:10:05.600
<v ARSENEAULT>Okay.

1930
02:10:05.600 --> 02:10:08.000
<v DELMA BENNETT>And my . . . I'm a scrapper too.

1931
02:10:08.000 --> 02:10:08.400
<v ARSENEAULT>Okay.

1932
02:10:08.400 --> 02:10:12.400
<v DELMA BENNETT>See like my truck got all that stuff on it?

1933
02:10:12.400 --> 02:10:14.000
<v ARSENEAULT>I didn't see.

1934
02:10:14.000 --> 02:10:16.128
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yeah, but I'm a scrapper.

1935
02:10:16.128 --> 02:10:17.405
I do recycling.

1936
02:10:17.405 --> 02:10:17.831
<v ARSENEAULT>Okay.

1937
02:10:17.831 --> 02:10:21.661
Do you remember any other local businesses in Mossville?

1938
02:10:21.661 --> 02:10:25.066
<v DELMA BENNETT>They had . . . Mossville was a little thriving community.

1939
02:10:25.066 --> 02:10:32.727
It was really . . . But most of the community, I mean most of the store owners were whites, though.

1940
02:10:32.727 --> 02:10:38.260
Most of the store owners was actually whites because they had grocery stores,

1941
02:10:38.260 --> 02:10:44.645
they had service stations . . . they had . . . grocery stores, and service stations, and a few restaurants.

1942
02:10:44.645 --> 02:10:47.198
They had a couple of restaurants.

1943
02:10:47.198 --> 02:10:49.752
Barbeque places and stuff like that.

1944
02:10:49.752 --> 02:10:55.711
They didn't have to go too far to get the things that they needed.

1945
02:10:55.711 --> 02:11:04.649
Then Walmart opened up over on Cities Service Highway, so that was a hop skip and a jump to get there.

1946
02:11:04.649 --> 02:11:08.054
So Mossville is in a very important area.

1947
02:11:08.054 --> 02:11:13.161
It's going to really be worth a lot in the near future,

1948
02:11:13.161 --> 02:11:23.376
but they have to get it at their price now in order to do what they have to do because they have bought property,

1949
02:11:23.376 --> 02:11:31.037
I’ve heard, that they have bought property and have sold it for double what they bought it from,

1950
02:11:31.037 --> 02:11:48.913
the Sasol, because they really say they don't need it right now but whenever they can get rid of it they get rid of it because the railroad bought some of the property they had bought and all that kind of stuff.

1951
02:11:48.913 --> 02:11:53.595
And they didn't sell it for the same amount that they

1952
02:11:53.595 --> 02:11:55.298
<c.p>paid for it, so.

1953
02:11:55.298 --> 02:11:57.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Where's your property?

1954
02:11:57.000 --> 02:12:00.793
<v DELMA BENNETT>My property is over on [Edna Hardy?] Lane.

1955
02:12:00.793 --> 02:12:04.111
It's right behind Mount Zion Baptist Church.

1956
02:12:04.111 --> 02:12:14.541
A tree fell on the building last year when the big storm came through in May and damaged it a little bit.

1957
02:12:14.541 --> 02:12:25.919
I got some people staying back there to maintain it for me until I decide to do what I'm going to do with it.

1958
02:12:25.919 --> 02:12:34.452
So I'm happy here for right now, but if I ever sell it I'll probably go to Texas.

1959
02:12:34.452 --> 02:12:44.881
I might even go . . . I can't go back to San Francisco because it just cost too much to live in San Francisco.

1960
02:12:44.881 --> 02:12:48.200
It costs to live in San Francisco.

1961
02:12:48.200 --> 02:12:52.467
To rent a basement apartment is fifteen hundred dollars.

1962
02:12:52.467 --> 02:12:58.156
When I was there I was only paying seventy-five dollars a month.

1963
02:12:58.156 --> 02:12:58.630
<v ARSENEAULT>Wow.

1964
02:12:58.630 --> 02:13:01.000
<v DELMA BENNETT>Back in the sixties.

1965
02:13:01.000 --> 02:13:04.153
<v ARSENEAULT>What was it like in the sixties?

1966
02:13:04.153 --> 02:13:05.053
Haight Street?

1967
02:13:05.053 --> 02:13:10.458
<v DELMA BENNETT>Oh don't even talk about it. [laughs] Don't even talk about it.

1968
02:13:10.458 --> 02:13:16.763
<v ARSENEAULT>Did you go on Haight Street? [Be?] good now, you were [in the military?].

1969
02:13:16.763 --> 02:13:19.015
<v DELMA BENNETT>[Went to?] Hippy Hill too.

1970
02:13:19.015 --> 02:13:21.718
You ever heard of Hippy Hill?

1971
02:13:21.718 --> 02:13:22.168
<v ARSENEAULT>[disagrees]

1972
02:13:22.168 --> 02:13:22.618
<v DELMA BENNETT>No?

1973
02:13:22.618 --> 02:13:25.321
Was on Haight Street, yes ma'am.

1974
02:13:25.321 --> 02:13:28.473
I was up and down Haight Street.

1975
02:13:28.473 --> 02:13:39.733
Most of the time I was in the service in the heat of things because from '65 to '67 I was in the army then,

1976
02:13:39.733 --> 02:13:42.435
but it started way before that.

1977
02:13:42.435 --> 02:13:52.794
Then '63 I was at San Francisco City College and I was devoting most of my time to playing football at the college.

1978
02:13:52.794 --> 02:13:55.947
If I wouldn't have dropped out O.J.

1979
02:13:55.947 --> 02:13:59.099
Simpson would have been my running back.

1980
02:13:59.099 --> 02:14:00.000
<v ARSENEAULT>Wow.

1981
02:14:00.000 --> 02:14:00.392
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yeah.

1982
02:14:00.392 --> 02:14:02.742
If I wouldn't have dropped out.

1983
02:14:02.742 --> 02:14:04.700
I dropped out in '65.

1984
02:14:04.700 --> 02:14:07.442
He came right after I dropped out.

1985
02:14:07.442 --> 02:14:10.575
I was in the army at that time.

1986
02:14:10.575 --> 02:14:16.450
I didn't get out until '67, but they were still . . . It was still a movement.

1987
02:14:16.450 --> 02:14:24.675
They still . . . The hippy movement was still going on in '67 all the way through '69 because I left in '69.

1988
02:14:24.675 --> 02:14:33.292
After I finished trade school I came back to Lake Charles because I wanted to start me a business in Lake Charles.

1989
02:14:33.292 --> 02:14:44.650
That's the only reason why I came back because I said if I was going to do something in life I wanted to be able to do it here,

1990
02:14:44.650 --> 02:14:50.525
and if I didn't make it here then I would go back to San Francisco.

1991
02:14:50.525 --> 02:14:54.833
Then I met my wife and I been here ever since.

1992
02:14:54.833 --> 02:14:57.183
I visit a couple of times.

1993
02:14:57.183 --> 02:15:01.100
I went last year . . . May of last year I went.

1994
02:15:01.100 --> 02:15:10.108
I was supposed to go today, but I didn't have the money to make the . . . I had the money to make the trip,

1995
02:15:10.108 --> 02:15:17.942
but I didn't want to go down for two days and spend over a thousand dollars just for two days.

1996
02:15:17.942 --> 02:15:24.600
Because one of my cousins, he's a preacher that died in San Francisco, and we didn't think

1997
02:15:24.600 --> 02:15:31.258
<c.p>that it would be feasible to spend that kind of money just to go for the funeral.

1998
02:15:31.258 --> 02:15:33.217
But they buried him today.

1999
02:15:33.217 --> 02:15:34.000
Yeah.

2000
02:15:34.000 --> 02:15:34.558
<v ARSENEAULT>Still talking.

2001
02:15:34.558 --> 02:15:36.233
<v DELMA BENNETT>[Thelma?] give me my phone please.

2002
02:15:36.233 --> 02:15:38.186
<v ARSENEAULT>We'll we're at two hours and twenty.

2003
02:15:38.186 --> 02:15:40.419
Do you want to call it a day?

2004
02:15:40.419 --> 02:15:40.977
<v DELMA BENNETT>Yes ma’am.

2005
02:15:40.977 --> 02:15:41.535
That's fine.

2006
02:15:41.535 --> 02:15:44.605
<v ARSENEAULT>Alright, well thank you so much for talking to us today.

2007
02:15:44.605 --> 02:15:44.884
<v DELMA BENNETT>Alright.

2008
02:15:44.884 --> 02:15:46.000
<v ARSENEAULT>It was good.

2009
02:15:46.000 --> 02:15:46.200
<c.p>[End Tape 4620.

2010
02:15:46.000 --> 02:15:46.200
End Session I.]
